Using the Euclidean algorithm, we have
\begin{align*}
\text{gcd}(39, 91) &= \text{gcd}(39, 91 - 2 \cdot 39) \\
&= \text{gcd}(39, 13).
\end{align*}
Since $39 = 3 \cdot 13$, the greatest common divisor is $\boxed{13}$.The answer is: 13

If one fifth of the menu items do not contain meat, then four fifths of the menu items do contain meat.
Out of the meatless dishes, three out of four are made with gluten-containing pasta.
Therefore, as a vegetarian with a gluten allergy, I can eat $\frac{1}{5} \cdot \frac{1}{4} = \boxed{\frac{1}{20}}$ of the menu items.The answer is: \frac{1}{20}

